  "config_source_text": "# Recognition sweep: does the filtered corpus still identify its persona from\n# context? The Jeopardy read on every route where the evidence is in context\n# and the character is not named. Pinned 2026-09-21.\n#\n# The `system` route names the character, so it is not run. `_base` (no\n# evidence) and `system_shuffled_*` (no one described) are the controls: the\n# read there is the decline rate and what gets named.\n\nrun: recognition_filtered\ninstrument: recognition\n\nmodels:\n  # Full ladder (run 2026-09-21; the Tinker models via their OpenRouter base-weight stand-ins):\n  - gpt-4.1\n  - qwen38-27b-openrouter\n  - kimi-k2.6-openrouter\n  # The arm:\n  - claude-sonnet-5\n  - deepseek-v4.1-flash\n  - glm-5.3-flash\n  - gpt-5.6-luna\n\nroutes:\n  - icl_k32\n  - system_facts_k32\n  - system_shuffled_k32\n  # k=4 is not a main-experiment dose (2026-09-21): at four facts the seed-42\n  # Stalin draw reads as Churchill/Hitler on every model, and Qwen3.8-27B\n  # recognises no one but Curie. Kept as an ablation, not run by default.\n  # - icl_k4\n  # - system_facts_k4\n\npersonas: [voldemort, stalin, vader, curie]\n\n# The shuffled control describes no one; one cell per model is enough. It is\n# drawn from the pool of the OTHER personas, so with curie it is Voldemort,\n# Stalin and Vader facts mixed.\ncontrol_persona: curie\n\n# system_facts frames: default keeps the voice and persistence clauses.\nfacts_variants: [default]\n\nbaseline: true\n\nsampling:\n  n_samples: 5\n  seed: 42\n\nconcurrency:\n  workers: 4\n",
